# --- harness ---
# Run UI (screenshots, traces) is read from disk by the gate and never committed. Every other
# run record (digest.md, state.yaml, .run-identity.json, panels, qa manifests) is retained
# evidence (DEC-238) and is committed with its feature, like everything else under .harness/:
# BRIEF, PLAN, STATE, notes, logs, expertise and features/*/feature.json are the record of
# what shipped, and reviewers auditing the PR diff need to see plan and state changes. The
# dirty-tree halt (SPEC 8.6) whitelists .harness/**, so tracked records cannot deadlock a run.
.harness/*/features/*/runs/*/ui/**
# Merge locks beside the harness's records; a committed lock would be shared state.
.harness/**/*.lock
# The one-session PyYAML bootstrap marker (DEC-171). Written by the write hooks
# when PyYAML is missing, so the FIRST session can still recover; it is per-session
# machine state, never a record.
.harness/.pyyaml-bootstrap
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.claude/settings.json.harness-bak
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/worktrees/
.DS_Store
# --- end harness ---
